    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1141">

                <pb facs="1509" n="1499" xml:id="pg1499"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EW/12–2445</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in Greece</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacVeagh</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-12-29T20:00:00-05:00">December 29,
                            1945—8 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1306. ReEmbtel 38 from Paris to Athens Dec 24, repeated to Dept as 7337. Please
                    make representation to FonOff as suggested by Angell urging Greek Govt to sign
                    final act Paris Conference on Reparation, if possible, before Jan 5. Dept making
                    similar representation Greek Ambassador here.<anchor n="18" xml:id="d1141-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Sent to Athens as 1306, repeated to Paris as Depts 6085 for Angell No. 120.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1141-f1" n="18" xml:id="d1141-f1-content">
                <p>Department’s telegram 2381, December 29, 7 p.m., to Cairo, not printed, urged
                    that similar representations be made to the Egyptian Government (740.00119
                    EW/12–2445).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
